---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: "How much does it cost?",
    a: "You start with a Sprint — €6,250 for two weeks, with full credit toward month 1 if you continue within 14 days. Ongoing arrangements after the Sprint are tailored to your product and scoped with you directly.",
  },
  {
    q: "How many sprints until I have a product?",
    a: "Honestly — it depends on what you're building. A focused tool might take one or two. A multi-user platform, more. What's true every time: the first Sprint produces something tangible you can put in front of users or investors, and you'll finish it knowing exactly what the path looks like. No open-ended retainers, no surprises.",
  },
  {
    q: "Who actually does the work?",
    a: "Tom reviews every meaningful product decision. Jakub leads engineering and reviews every meaningful piece of code. Senior engineers do the build; AI agents handle boilerplate, tests, and infrastructure underneath. We don't grow by rotating juniors onto your project.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can we pause?",
    a: "Yes. If you need to pause, you can — banked time converts to maintenance work like security patches, App Store submissions and small fixes while you decide what's next. We don't use it as a sales hook, but it's there as a reassurance.",
  },
  {
    q: "Do you take equity?",
    a: "No. Fixed fee. You keep all of the upside.",
  },
  {
    q: "What about IP ownership?",
    a: "Everything we build is yours. Code, designs, assets, App Store accounts — all transferred at handover. No lock-in.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can you work with our existing codebase?",
    a: "Yes. We regularly pick up projects mid-stream, audit existing code, fix security debt, and improve what's already there. We play well with other teams too — no takeover, no politics.",
  },
  {
    q: "What if we hate the work?",
    a: "If a build is going the wrong way we'll re-plan mid-cycle rather than power through. The Sprint exists exactly so neither side commits before there's evidence — if it's not working after the Sprint, we shake hands and part ways.",
  },
];
---

<section class="bg-cream py-24 md:py-[120px]">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1180px] px-6">

    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-coral mb-6 md:mb-8">FAQ</p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-5xl md:text-6xl text-navy leading-tight tracking-tight max-w-lg mb-16">
      You're probably wondering...
    </h2>

    <div class="flex flex-col" style="border-top: 1px solid #d8d0a8;">
      {faqs.map((faq) => (
        <details class="group border-b" style="border-color: #d8d0a8;">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none py-6 gap-4">
            <span class="font-sans font-medium text-base text-navy pr-4">{faq.q}</span>
            <span class="faq-plus shrink-0 w-6 h-6 rounded-full border border-navy-muted flex items-center justify-center text-navy transition-transform duration-200">
              <svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 10 10" fill="none">
                <path d="M5 1v8M1 5h8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
              </svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <p class="pb-6 text-sm text-navy-muted leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">{faq.a}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
